1
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:12,167
This is the story of Joe and Fonzie.

2
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:18,030
It’s a story about a friendship that started more than 20 years ago.

3
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:27,060
It’s also a story about a friendship that saved a life and started a new kind of help for people with problems.

4
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:34,168
‘Joe’ is Joe Hoagland, who was three years old when the story began.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,160
And ‘Fonzie’ is a 3-metre-long, 275 kilogram dolphin.

6
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:49,563
When Joe was born, he had a problem with his heart and doctors had to operate on him.

7
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:53,200
When he was three, he had another operation.

8
00:00:54,360 --> 00:01:01,812
This operation didn’t go well and he became paralysed – he couldn’t move the left side of his body.

9
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,827
The doctors at the hospital didn’t think he could get better.

10
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:14,780
Deena, Joe’s mother, took him to different places for therapy, but it wasn’t very successful.

11
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:18,200
Then the family moved to Florida.

12
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:24,544
Joe liked being in the water and Deena thought swimming could help him.

13
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:32,903
First, they went to swimming pools in hotels, but some hotel guests didn’t like them being there.

14
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:42,740
Then one day she went with Joe to a place in Key Largo called Dolphin Plus, where people swam with dolphins.

15
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:48,320
Joe met Fonzie there and the story really began.

16
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:53,660
Soon, Joe wanted to see Fonzie every day.

17
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:57,133
He loved playing with him and feeding him.

18
00:01:57,940 --> 00:02:02,067
Every time that Joe arrived, Fonzie came to see him.

19
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:12,865
Joe’s mother told him always to feed Fonzie using his left hand, so Joe used his left side more and more.

20
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:16,173
Slowly, he got better and better.

21
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,783
He’s now over 30 years old and very well.

22
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:30,920
Deena saw that Joe’s friendship with Fonzie helped him a lot, and she knew it was a good idea for other people, too.

23
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:37,880
So, she and her family worked to open a place called Island Dolphin Care.

24
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:45,580
It’s next to Dolphin Plus and many people with health problems come to spend time with the dolphins.

25
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:51,860
Sadly, Fonzie died in 2004 when Joe was 17.

26
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:59,140
He wrote: ‘Fonzie was a great friend to me; he and I shared a lot of good times.

27
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:01,940
He always put a smile on my face.’
